// Title: WinSxS Executable File Creation By Non-System Process
// Sigma ID: 34746e8c-5fb8-415a-b135-0abc167e912a
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-11 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects the creation of binaries in the WinSxS folder by non-system processes
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://media.defense.gov/2023/May/09/2003218554/-1/-1/0/JOINT_CSA_HUNTING_RU_INTEL_SNAKE_MALWARE_20230509.PDF
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_winsxs_binary_creation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\" and FolderPath endswith ".exe") and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\Systems32\\" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\")))
